{
  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_015: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat → 0.619 acc). The most critical uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion actually adds value over a single-modality baseline. config_023 (image_only, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool) is the cleanest single-variable comparison: it keeps the same image encoder (resnet50), profile setting (multiprofile), and aggregation (avgpool), differing only in the removal of the RNA modality. If image-only performance is close to 0.619, the RNA modality contributes little and we should focus on image encoder quality; if it is substantially lower, RNA is a meaningful contributor and we can exploit multimodal directions. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design decision (multimodal vs. unimodal) under a limited budget, and avoids changing multiple variables simultaneously."
}

